            <ArticleTitle>Technical considerations in deploying the sheathed Palmaz-Schatz stent in distal coronary artery and bypass graft lesions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The deliverable catheter length of the Palmaz-Schatz stent delivery system is significantly limited by the protective sheath and clamshell device. This limitation must be considered when planning distal stent placement, especially in bypass graft lesions. A technique for shortening the guide catheter without losing guidewire position is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
